  "data": {
    "document": "Core Rules",
    "section": "15. Stratagems",
    "ruleNumber": "15.01",
    "summary": "A Stratagem lists its price, timing, eligible targets, effect and any extra restrictions. Core Stratagems are available to everyone. Codexes and other releases supply more. Each player can reuse a Stratagem across the battle, with a maximum of one use per phase. Separately, each player may direct just one Stratagem at a given unit in a phase unless a rule overrides that cap. Choose the targets, deduct the price from your pool (see Gain Core CP), then apply the effect. You need enough CP to use it. A bonus priced separately, for example at +1 CP, applies only if you pay the surcharge. A modifier cannot drop the price past 0 CP. A change triggered by using the Stratagem applies to that instance alone. Target selection makes the unit count as affected. Ownership language refers to the Stratagems available to the player in question. When an effect says “your unit”, it means only the chosen target units, even if you have other units in your army.",
